# The WebAssembly plugin host in the application (PLAN.md §13.6 row 96): PluginLoader.LoadAll at
# start over the plugins folder (Plugin/PluginLoader.cs:203-311), each plugin on its own thread,
# its map menu entries in the map menus and its questions over the window.
#
# The claim: two of the C#'s example plugins, ported to the WIT world and built for WebAssembly,
# are laid in the plugins folder before start - FenceDist (plugins/example3-fencedist.cs) and
# "Small stuff" (plugins/example2-menu.cs). Both load and run, and the status line carries the
# loader's "Plugin Init <name> <version> by <author>"; "Draw Fence Dist" is on the flight map's
# plugin entries and "Fix mission top/bottom" at the end of the planning map's right-click menu.
# Choosing the latter shows the example's message box, then its "Enter Angle" input box; 90 and
# Enter put two DO_SET_SERVOs at the top of the empty mission and two at the bottom - four rows
# made through the plan's own AddCommand.
#
# The folder is the run's own through MP_PLUGINS, so no plugin is left beside the shared binary.
# The setup builds the two plugins (cargo, wasm32-unknown-unknown; a machine without that target
# does not run this test) and copies them there. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/plugins.gui

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 8
# A first budget, set by hand until a passing run records one.
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
env MP_PLUGINS $WORK/plugins
setup cargo build -q --release -p mp-plugins --target wasm32-unknown-unknown --example fencedist --example menu
setup mkdir -p $WORK/plugins && cp "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/examples/fencedist.wasm" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/examples/menu.wasm" $WORK/plugins/

# Loaded, in the folder's name order: fencedist.wasm is plugin 0, menu.wasm plugin 1.
expect plugins.count 2
expect plugins.FenceDist.state running
expect plugins.FenceDist.version 0.10
expect plugins.FenceDist.author Michael Oborne
expect plugins.Small_stuff.state running
expect status ~ Plugin Init
expect plugins.menu.flight-data Draw Fence Dist
expect plugins.menu.flight-planner Fix mission top/bottom
expect plugins.question none

# The planning map's menu, the plugin's entry at its end.
click tab-plan
expect map.ready true
expect mission.items 0
click map@0.40x0.50:right
click plugin-menu-1-0
expect plan.menu closed
expect plugins.question ~ This is a sample plugin
click plugin-question-ok
expect plugins.question ~ Enter Angle
type 90
key Return
expect plugins.question none
expect mission.items 4
expect mission.commands 183,183,183,183
